2026-11-10  Carsten Bormann  <cabo@tzi.org>

	* 0.6.2.2: Safer decode defaults (BREAKING).  Object-constructing
	tags are no longer reconstructed into live Ruby objects by default,
	because CBOR.decode is commonly run on input from untrusted sources.
	Tag 35 (Regexp) and tag 32 (URI) now decode to a generic CBOR::Tagged
	value instead of building a Regexp or URI from the decoded value.  A
	caller that trusts the source opts in per tag:

	    CBOR.decode(data)                                   # CBOR::Tagged
	    CBOR.decode(data, reconstruct_from_tags: [CBOR::TAG_REGEXP])
	    CBOR.decode(data, reconstruct_from_tags: [CBOR::TAG_URI])

	Module constants CBOR::TAG_REGEXP (35) and CBOR::TAG_URI (32) are
	provided; bare integers are also accepted.  Tag 0/1 (time) stays on
	by default, as reconstructing a Time from an epoch is a plain value
	conversion.  The option works for both CBOR.decode and Unpacker.new,
	like the existing symbolize_keys option.  This mirrors the principle
	behind YAML.safe_load and JSON.parse(create_additions: false):
	turning wire data into live objects should be opt-in.

